1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
Voltage connects existing e-commerce operations to agents through WebMCP.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:14,000
We begin with the oldest pending refund approval.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:23,000
One business instruction asks the agent to verify the evidence
and prepare a reversible review note.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:30,000
The agent discovers route-aware tools exposed by the current page.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Agent processing condensed for time.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:49,000
The agent identifies APR-2006 / RMA-2006
and opens the approval workspace.

7
00:00:49,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Eligibility, inspection, the immutable calculation,
amount, and data versions are checked.

8
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:14,000
The evidence agrees: one accepted item and a USD 7.99 refund.

9
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:28,000
A recommendation is drafted under the signed-in user's account.

10
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:43,000
The agent stops here. It cannot publish the note,
approve the request, or execute the refund.

11
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:58,000
The reviewer checks the evidence in the existing application.

12
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:12,000
The reviewer publishes the note and records the final approval manually.

13
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:22,000
A second agent check re-discovers the tools available on the current page.

14
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:36,000
The RMA now reflects the approved state across modules.

15
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:48,000
The workflow advances to refund execution
with the same USD 7.99 calculation.

16
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:55,000
The final refund action remains a human responsibility.
